WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
In English, the word
"the" never changes.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:09.610
In Spanish, it does: el libro,
la casa, los libros, las casas.

3
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.150
A book isn't male.

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.130
A house isn't female.

5
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.490
Then a map, ending in the
letter a just like a house,

6
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.050
takes a different word: el mapa.

7
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.630
So what decides which
"the" a Spanish noun gets?

8
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.630
In this mission, you'll find
the clues a noun carries,

9
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.310
and the exceptions
worth learning by heart.

10
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.030
You'll make the feminine
of words for people,

11
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.300
turn one thing into many, and
join two little words into one:

12
00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.350
de and el.

13
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:41.550
Your mission: crack the code
behind every Spanish "the".
